00:52:56,470 --> 00:53:02,470
Paradise Now (Arabic: الجنّة الآن, romanized: al-Janna al-Laan) is a
2005 psychological drama film directed by Hany Abu-Assad.

11
00:58:14,117 --> 00:58:20,117
It follows the story of two Palestinian men
preparing for a suicide attack in Israel.

12
01:03:31,764 --> 01:03:37,764
The film won the Golden Globe Award for Best Foreign Language Film and
received an Academy Award nomination in the same category.

13
01:08:49,411 --> 01:08:55,411
According to Abu-Assad, "The film is an artistic
point of view of that political issue.

14
01:14:07,058 --> 01:14:13,058
The politicians want to see it as black and white, good and
evil, and art wants to see it as a human thing."

15
01:19:24,705 --> 01:19:30,705
The film explores themes of individual, friendship, israel,
palestinian-israeli conflict, palestine.

16
01:24:42,352 --> 01:24:48,352
The tone is emotional and intense.
